2026-09-27T03:27:30.2375077Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2375429Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2375965Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2376940Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2377816Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2377907Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2378106Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2378380Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2378639Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2378724Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2378977Z ================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2379126Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2379318Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2379807Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2380110Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2380248Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2380609Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2380834Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2381017Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2381438Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2381785Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2382469Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2383030Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2383130Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2383582Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2384131Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2384441Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2384740Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2385127Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2385214Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2385428Z ========
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2386190Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2388072Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2390482Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2390893Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2391676Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2392503Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2393787Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2394938Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2396482Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2396944Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2397616Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2398193Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2476979Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2478614Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2480178Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2480950Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2481859Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2482287Z 
